nodes.body:
@DarkLight1337 @patrickvonplaten Thanks for linking #41948. I checked the overlap, and I think this PR is still useful.

#41948 fixes the Pixtral/Mistral processor compatibility path. This PR fixes the offline Mistral3 example itself: the current example passes raw [IMG], which can be tokenized as normal text instead of the actual Mistral image token. Switching the example to the Mistral chat/tokenizer path makes the example match how the model expects image placeholders to be inserted.

Since this is example-only and does not change core vLLM behavior, I think it can be merged independently of #41948.

